<title>USA: Coca-Cola Enterprises sets 3-for-1 split.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola Enterprises sets 3-for-1 split.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA, Ga. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coca-Cola Enterprises Inc said on Tuesday it set a three-for-one stock split, subject to shareholder approval.</p>
<p>The split, if approved, would be effective for holders of record on May 1. The company has about 125.7 million shares outstanding. They were trading at 60-7/8 at midday Tuesday.</p>
<p>If the split is approved, the company said it expects to maintain the quarterly dividend at $0.025 per share.</p>
<p>Coca-Cola Enterprises distributes almost 60 percent of the Coca-Cola Company's U.S. bottle and can production.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
